-- a recorded cost is read through annotations and applications to the head
-- the store's model has the shape of the table's, with the machine's own figures
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the cost model and the choice rule (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.14 “F33 — Navigation: the concrete form” and §15 “Open threads”)
-- The decision (2026-11-06). A cost model is a value of three measures and their weights: the
-- steps the machine recorded for the calls a term makes (through %gsteps, or a table), the term's
-- size (what building it costs), and a latency estimate from a schedule (where each global runs:
-- on the net, compiled, or across a foreign boundary). A purpose is a value: reach a term a
-- predicate accepts (a goal), minimize the model's cost, or reach a goal at least cost. The
-- choice rule is best-first: the frontier ordered by the model's cost of each reachable term, ties
-- by the term's key (its canonical serialization, compared as a list of words), so the choice
-- never depends on the order of the view; a visited set keeps the search from cycling; the
-- budget bounds the expansions. Validity never enters: every term reached is equal to the start
-- by the identities in view.
-- weights by repeated addition (weights are small words)
wtimes a n = if %weq n #0 then #0 else %wadd a (wtimes a (%wsub n #1))
